<article class="prose-izumi"><p class="eyebrow">Companion</p><h1>Troubleshooting</h1><p class="lede">Most setup problems come down to the TV, installer, and computer not being on the same network or the TV’s developer mode being stale.</p>
<h2>Installer cannot connect</h2><p>Confirm both devices are on the same Wi‑Fi or Ethernet network, Developer Mode is enabled, and Host PC IP matches the computer’s current local address. Restart the TV after changing it. If on-TV updates were enabled, temporarily change <code>127.0.0.1</code> back to the computer address before reconnecting.</p>
<h2>Installation failed</h2><p>Open the installer’s installation logs and check the Samsung error code. On TVs without updater support, disable <strong>Updates on your TV</strong> and install Companion only.</p>
<h2>No playable source</h2><p>Open izumi, refresh the source list, and try an HTTP or debrid result. Raw P2P and device-only sources require the paired izumi client. If a stream resolves but does not start, choose a different codec or subtitle variant.</p>
<h2>Still stuck?</h2><p><a href="https://github.com/nickEatsBread/izumiCompanion/issues">Open an issue</a> with your TV model, Tizen version, Companion version, and relevant logs. Never attach signing identities, API keys, or account tokens.</p></article>
